}

docs {
  # Assign Mentor to ASH Student

  Assigns a mentor to an ASH student registration record by updating the `assignedMentor` field. On success, all ASH student cache entries (single records and paginated lists matching `cedarrise:ash:ashStudents:*`) are invalidated.

  ## Authorization
  Requires `update` permission.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Parameter | Type     | Required | Description                    |
  |-----------|----------|----------|--------------------------------|
  | `id`      | `string` | Yes      | UUID of the ASH student record.|

  ## Request Body (`form-urlencoded`)

  | Field    | Type     | Required | Validation    | Description                      |
  |----------|----------|----------|---------------|----------------------------------|
  | `mentor` | `string` | Yes      | Min 3 chars   | Full name of the mentor to assign.|

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`** — Returns the updated student record with `id`, `status`, and `assignedMentor`.

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Mentor assigned to Ash student successfully",
    "data": {
      "id": "uuid",
      "status": "accepted",
      "assignedMentor": "Sampson"
    },
    "meta": {
      "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
    }
  }
  ```

  | Field            | Type     | Description                                    |
  |------------------|--------|--------------------------------------------------|
  | `id`             | `string` | UUID of the updated ASH student record.        |
  | `status`         | `string` | Current admin status of the student.           |
  | `assignedMentor` | `string` | Name of the newly assigned mentor.             |

  ## Side Effects
  - Emits `ASH_EVENTS.DELETE_CACHE` to invalidate pattern `cedarrise:ash:ashStudents:*`.

  ## Errors

  | Status                      | Description                                              |
  |-----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Invalid `id` format or `mentor` missing/too short.       |
  | `401 Unauthorized`          | Missing or invalid authentication token.                 |
  | `403 Forbidden`             | User does not have `update` permission.                  |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                                 |
}
